To run this project, you cannot simply double-click the files. Because it uses PHP and MySQL, you need a local server environment.

Here is the step-by-step guide to running this on your Windows, Mac, or Linux computer using XAMPP (the easiest free tool for this).

Step 1: Install XAMPP
Download XAMPP from apachefriends.org.

Install it.

Open the XAMPP Control Panel.

Click "Start" next to Apache (the web server) and MySQL (the database).

Step 2: Create the Project Folder
Go to your XAMPP installation folder (usually C:\xampp on Windows).

Open the htdocs folder.

Create a new folder inside htdocs named gov_portal.

Step 3: Save the Files
Save the code I provided in the previous answer into that gov_portal folder with these exact names:

config.php

setup.php

index.php

admin.php

Step 4: Create the Uploads Folder (Important!)
Inside your gov_portal folder, create a new empty folder named:

uploads

If you skip this, image uploads will fail.

Step 5: Run the Auto-Installer
Now, open your web browser (Chrome, Edge, etc.) and type this URL: 👉 http://localhost/gov_portal/setup.php

You should see a green success message: "System Installed Successfully".

This automatically creates your Database and Tables. You don't need to touch phpMyAdmin.

Step 6: Use the Website
1. Citizen View (Public): Go to: http://localhost/gov_portal/index.php

Fill out the form.

Upload a photo.

Copy the Docket ID (e.g., GOV-2024-X99) to track it later.

2. Admin View (Government): Go to: http://localhost/gov_portal/admin.php

Username: admin

Password: admin123

Here you can see the reports, view the photos, and change status to "Action Taken".

Troubleshooting
"Database Connection Failed": Open config.php and make sure $password is empty ("") if you are using default XAMPP. If you set a password for MySQL, update it there.

Images not uploading: Check if the uploads folder exists in C:\xampp\htdocs\gov_portal\